<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kwantung Oblast</h1><p class="st-meta">1898 CE – 1905 CE · capital Port Arthur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Russia's leased territory at the tip of the Liaodong peninsula, home of the Port Arthur naval base, lost to Japan in the Russo-Japanese War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/triple-intervention">Triple Intervention</a> forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> to give up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> peninsula in 1895, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> obtained a twenty-five-year lease of its southern tip from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> in 1898. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> fortified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Port Arthur</a> as an ice-free Pacific naval base and built a commercial port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalian">Dalny</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The territory was linked to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harbin">Harbin</a> by the southern branch of the Chinese Eastern Railway. It was governed by military officers, and in 1903 Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yevgeny-alekseyev">Yevgeny Alekseyev</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Port Arthur</a>, became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-far-east">Russian Far East</a>. Russian advance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> alarmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and led directly to war.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Port Arthur</a> in February 1904. After a costly siege, the fortress commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatoly-stessel">Anatoly Stessel</a> surrendered in January 1905. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-portsmouth">Treaty of Portsmouth</a> transferred the lease to Japan, which renamed it the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kwantung-leased-territory">Kwantung Leased Territory</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1898 CE – 1905 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.47%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1898 CE – 1905 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Port Arthur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yevgeny Alekseyev, Anatoly Stessel</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Eastern Orthodoxy</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian, Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Russian Dalny, Kwantung Province (Russian)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1902&amp;focus=kwantung-oblast" aria-label="Kwantung Oblast on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7427 980 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kwantung Oblast lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6487 457h0M8529 1145h0M8013 1030h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7747 1236h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7747 1236h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day China. <a href="/atlas?year=1902&amp;focus=kwantung-oblast">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
